    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get the \"biological effect size\" angle, but even then, investors are going to look at the p-value on the slide. if they see 0.06, they're gonna see \"not significant.\" \n\ncan we just... smooth that over? instead of putting the actual p-value on the main impact slide, maybe we just say the results reached statistical significance or that the findings are \"statistically validated\" by the trend? i'm not saying we lie, i'm just saying we don't lead with the one number that could kill the deal. what do you think?",
